1
00:00:00,192 --> 00:00:02,652
(Leonard:)He lives in the same room
where his bassinet was.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:06,700
(Beverley:)Both selective mutism and an inability
to separate from one's mother...

3
00:00:06,866 --> 00:00:09,156
(Beverley:)...can stem from a pathological fear
of women.

4
00:00:09,702 --> 00:00:13,622
(Beverley:)It might explain why the two of you have
created an ersatz homosexual marriage...

5
00:00:13,789 --> 00:00:16,209
(Beverley:)...to satisfy your need for intimacy.

6
00:00:23,883 --> 00:00:25,343
(Howard:)Say what?

7
00:00:25,718 --> 00:00:26,718
[WHISPERS INAUDIBLY]

8
00:00:26,886 --> 00:00:29,266
(Howard:)That's basically what I just said.

9
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:32,180
(Leonard:)You brought your husband to work,
you know the rules.

10
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:36,730
[AS JAR JAR BINKS]
Meesa thinking yousa looking pretty sad...

11
00:00:36,896 --> 00:00:37,936
(Leonard:)...now too, betcha, betcha.

12
00:00:38,564 --> 00:00:42,194
Leonard, it's 1:00. Weren't you going
to show me your laboratory at 1:00?

13
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:45,900
(Leonard:)No hurry, Mother. Tell them more
about their secret love for each other.

14
00:00:46,072 --> 00:00:49,242
But it's 1:00. You were going to show me
your laboratory at 1:00.

15
00:00:49,408 --> 00:00:52,578
Her reasoning is unassailable. It is 1:00.

16
00:00:54,622 --> 00:00:56,202
(Leonard:)Fine. Let's go.

17
00:00:57,583 --> 00:00:59,753
(Leonard:)I think you'll find my work
pretty interesting.

18
00:00:59,919 --> 00:01:01,299
(Leonard:)I'm attempting to replicate...

